From: Ottsel A1.0
Subject: bounded GOAL->GOAL call trace probe (temporary diagnostic)

The goalc IR_FunctionCall shim records (call-site address, target GOAL
pointer) for every GOAL->GOAL call into a C ring buffer; the gated handler
dumps the last 48 calls, the last call target's code words, and the caller's
return address region at fault time.  This localized the object-204 (mood
-tables) fault below the full boot loop deterministically: one boot shows the
chain mood-tables top-level -> 0x23d8554 -> 0x23d8004 (loop) -> 0x5ab0e4 ->
0x5fc574/0x5fd9d4 -> 0x5a9234 (called repeatedly from site 0x23d8408), then
a jump to EE base (x8 = lr = 0x7000000000, signal 10).

IMPORTANT shim invariants (learned during A1.0):
- The recorder is a C call: it clobbers x8-x15 and x30, so the shim must
  push/pop x0-x15 + x16/x17 around the recorder (a first version pushed only
  x0-x7, x16, x17 and the function pointer living in x8 was destroyed ->
  calls jumped to garbage).
- The recorder's own address is resolved through a symbol slot using the
  IR_LoadSymbolPointer/IR_SetSymbolValue pattern: (sym-s7) from the slot,
  + st, + offset (EE base) BEFORE reading the symbol's value, then + offset
  again for the code address.  Missing the first +offset reads the GOAL-
  relative symbol address as a host address (SIGSEGV in the shim itself).
- The call-site capture uses `adr x1, .` (per-call-site address).  Caveat:
  validate-arm64-emission.py's PC-relative round-trip reassembler mishandles
  ADR (byte immediate, no >>2) -- the probe build reports ADR round-trip
  mismatches.  The instructions are legal A64 (clang assembles them
  identically); the validator limitation is irrelevant once the probe is
  stripped (the product build validates clean).

Reapply temporarily when debugging GAME.CGO boot faults; strip before any
product commit.

--- out/jak-project/game/kernel/jak1/kscheme.cpp	2026-08-09 13:54:42
+++ /tmp/probe_kscheme.cpp	2026-08-09 13:54:37
@@ -28,6 +28,24 @@
 #include "game/mips2c/mips2c_table.h"
 
 using namespace jak1_symbols;
+
+// Ottsel A1.0 bounded call trace (TEMPORARY diagnostic): every GOAL->GOAL
+// call records (call-site host addr, target GOAL ptr) into a ring buffer so
+// the gated handler can dump the last calls before the object-204
+// ret-to-EE-base fault.  Global namespace (NOT anonymous) so the extern "C"
+// decls in src/shell/ios_boot.cpp link.  Removed once the first bad
+// transition is identified.
+extern "C" {
+constexpr int OTTSEL_CALL_TRACE_N = 256;
+volatile u64 g_ottsel_call_trace[OTTSEL_CALL_TRACE_N];
+volatile u64 g_ottsel_call_idx = 0;
+
+void ottsel_trace_goal_call(u64 target, u64 site) {
+  u64 idx = __atomic_fetch_add(&g_ottsel_call_idx, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED);
+  g_ottsel_call_trace[idx % OTTSEL_CALL_TRACE_N] =
+      ((u64)(site & 0xffffffff) << 32) | (target & 0xffffffff);
+}
+}  // extern "C"
 
